## Section voice guide

### Abstract (220–250 words)

Thesis abstract: full ladder + synthetic + LOSO numbers.  
**Paper abstract:** problem (cross-lab MSSV) → approach (decoder-only cHMM–GMVAE, zero-shot holdout) → **one headline number** (mean NMI 0.58 vs 0.28) → substage/K-sweep in one clause. No citations.

Template:
> [Clinical/method gap]. [Gap in prior supervised/unsupervised work]. We [approach in one sentence]. On [cohort/protocol], [model A] [verb] [model B] ([numbers]). [One sentence substages/limitations].

### Introduction (350–450 words)

Follow thesis §1.1–1.2 **logic**, not length:

1. Sleep staging matters; mouse model; **cross-lab variability** (Rose MSSV).
2. Supervised CNNs need labels/retraining; transductive tools need per-mouse calibration.
3. Unsupervised + temporal structure (HMM tradition, mcRBM substages) — **missing piece**: zero-shot cross-lab holdout without calibration.
4. **Contributions (i)(ii)(iii)** — mirror thesis “validation ladder” but for holdout paper.

Use `\methodpara` only in Data/Methods, not Intro.

### Data (~300–400 words)

Thesis Ch. 2 style: **numbers before models**. Your thesis excels at cohort tables — replicate as `\methodpara{Dataset.}`, `{Preprocessing.}`, `{Inputs.}` with mice counts, hours, montage, screening thresholds.

### Methods (~900–1,100 words)

Thesis Methods tone: precise, reproducible, impersonal.  
Pattern per block:

```
\methodpara{Label.}
[What is done — one sentence scope].
[How — architecture/training with symbols already defined].
[Holdout-specific rule — what is OFF at inference].
[Pointer to SI for locks/ablations — one clause].
```

Minimal equations (encoder, decoder, Viterbi, NMI) — thesis had many more; paper keeps four max.

### Results and discussion (~900–1,100 words)

**Your thesis Results formula** (keep this — it reads as you):

```
In Table/Fig X, [observation with number].
[Comparison — vs baseline, vs chance, vs other fold, vs thesis LOSO if contrast].
[Mechanistic reading — montage, prior type, cohort size, label noise].
[One-clause limitation if needed].
```

Subsections (paper): Cross-lab holdout → Laboratory heterogeneity → Substage resolution → Methodological implications.  
Thesis had *Why X breaks* subsubsections — **merge into paragraph 3** above.

### Conclusion (120–180 words)

Thesis Conclusion §6 style: synthesise ladder outcomes in **3–5 sentences**, no new numbers, no future-work essay. One sentence limitation max.

