## Canonical terminology (use consistently)

| Prefer | Avoid |
|--------|--------|
| Wake, NREM, REM (capitals for stages) | wake/nrem/rem inconsistent casing |
| prior NMI | WandB KMeans NMI (auxiliary only) |
| holdout / held-out mice | test set (unless defined) |
| mixture prior / mixture component | cluster (OK but less precise) |
| decoder-only conditioning | decoder only (hyphenate adjective) |
| cHMM–GMVAE (en-dash) | cHMMGMVAE in prose (OK in tables) |
| laboratories 2, 3, and 5 | lab2/lab3 shorthand in prose |
| zero-shot (holdout without subject ID) | zero shot |
| label-agnostic / unsupervised | fully unsupervised (we use expert labels for **evaluation**) |
| nuisance (subject, montage) | noise (ambiguous) |

Acronyms: define once — EEG, EMG, NMI, MSSV, cGMVAE, cHMM–GMVAE, HMMGMVAE.

